    "text_full": "Cookie Settings\nMain Content\nMain Menu\nSEARCH\nMENU\nPeople\nPractices\nInsights\nLATEST POSTS\nABOUT\nCONTRIBUTORS\nCATEGORIES\nSEARCH WILEY CONNECT\nFEATURED POSTS\nMay 19, 2026\nAI in Hiring: Evolving Legal Risks Under State and Federal Law\nAI & Machine Learning\nPrivacy + Cybersecurity\n\nEmployers are increasingly integrating artificial intelligence (AI) into the hiring process, deploying AI hiring tools across multiple stages of the employment funnel, including to manage application volume.\n\nThese tools promise efficiency, but they also raise potential legal risks related to disparate impact discrimination and compliance with other legal requirements when automated systems influence employment outcomes. Use of these technologies is also ripe for novel lawsuits, raising litigation risks for employers.\n\nBelow we lay out key state, local, and federal approaches to regulating AI in hiring and provide practical guidance for employers to navigate and manage growing risk in this area.\n\nMay 8, 2026\nThe FCC's Expanding Role in National Security\nSpectrum Policy\nWiley Connected Podcast\nMay 4, 2026\nZero Day Factory: How to Manage Risks from New AI-Driven Vulnerability Discovery Capabilities\nAI & Machine Learning\nPrivacy + Cybersecurity\nApril 30, 2026\nUtah Amends App Store Accountability Act (ASAA) – Key Obligations Delayed Until May 6, 2027\nPrivacy + Cybersecurity\nAll\nAI & Machine Learning\nConnected Cars\nConnected Health\nDigital Assets, Cryptocurrencies, and Blockchain\nFTC Consumer Protection and Privacy Enforcement Series\nInternet of Things\nPrivacy + Cybersecurity\nSpace and Satellite\n+ Load More\n\nSubscribe to receive the latest updates from Wiley Connect\n\nSUBSCRIBE\nApril 28, 2026\nManaging Agentic AI in Real‑World Use: From Outputs to Actions\nAI & Machine Learning\nPrivacy + Cybersecurity\nApril 17, 2026\nCongress Again Approaches Deadline for Extending FISA 702 Authorities, Creating Uncertainty for Communications Pro